/P 79 0 R
/E (Zara's global supply chain has to deal with changing trade and regulatory environments. The Multi-Fiber Arrangement \(MFA\) made tariffs and quotas unclear. This had an effect on delivery schedules and the costs of finding suppliers. To grow into new markets, Zara had to deal with complicated methods to enter. For example, they had to deal with a failed joint venture in Italy before they could work with Percassi and open franchises in riskier parts of the Middle East. When doing business outside Europe, they have to deal with different import rules, labeling requirements, and paperwork. This slows down shipments from Spain and causes time delays.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
