/P 79 0 R
/E (Zara's business model is affected by the state of the world economy. Rising fuel prices and shipping costs around the world make it more expensive to send clothes from Arteixo. As the company moves into markets that are farther away, these transportation costs rise too quickly, putting the low prices that are necessary for it to stay competitive at risk. Zara is also at risk of losing money in foreign currencies because it only has one cost center that uses euros. A strong Euro makes its goods more expensive in other currencies, which makes it harder for them to compete on price in places like the Americas and Asia.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
