/P 79 0 R
/E (Zara's business model is based on how Europeans shop. Spanish shoppers buy a lot and does not care as much about global brands. Germans care more about price, and French shoppers care more about style and quality. This affects how Zara prices and makes its products. The company only spends 0.3% of its sales on advertising and relies on store-led marketing to bring in customers. It does this by using location and window displays. This method works in Europe, but it's riskier in developing markets where people don't know much about Zara.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
