/P 79 0 R
/E (Zara's use of airfreight to reach faraway markets raises its costs, environmental impact, and operational risks. Its fast-fashion model cuts down on waste in Europe, but slower international deliveries can leave many stock in other countries. The company is also under more and more pressure from the public and NGOs to keep a closer eye on its global supply chain. Its new Zaragoza logistics hub adds capacity, but it doesn't fix the main environmental problem with its long-haul shipping.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
